From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:33:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: fusb301: end the host role when the port becomes
 sink-only

Writing "sink" to port_type while a sink partner is attached turned the
host role and VBUS off for one poll only. The FUSB301 appears not to end
an attach on a Mode write: it kept reporting the sink it was sourcing
until the cable moved, and the next poll, with the cached status cleared
by the port type change, turned the host role and VBUS back on.

A sink-only port cannot serve a sink, so treat that report as a detach.
---
 drivers/usb/typec/fusb301.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/fusb301.c b/drivers/usb/typec/fusb301.c
index 02a1a9c43..19e68e22b 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/fusb301.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/fusb301.c
@@ -245,7 +245,13 @@ static int fusb301_update_status(struct fusb301 *fusb)
 	fusb->last_type = type;
 	fusb->last_valid = true;
 
-	if (!(status & FUSB301_STATUS_ATTACH)) {
+	/*
+	 * A Mode write does not end an attach: after a switch to sink-only the
+	 * chip keeps reporting the sink it was sourcing until the cable moves.
+	 * A sink-only port cannot serve a sink, so treat that as a detach.
+	 */
+	if (!(status & FUSB301_STATUS_ATTACH) ||
+	    (fusb->port_type == TYPEC_PORT_SNK && (type & FUSB301_TYPE_SINK))) {
 		fusb301_set_host(fusb, false);
 		fusb301_unregister_partner(fusb);
 		fusb->partner_type = 0;
-- 
2.43.0

